1
00:00:00,496 --> 00:00:14,000
Section 2 You will hear a talk given by a woman called Shona Ferguson about changes in a town called Barford.

2
00:00:14,714 --> 00:00:54,680
First, you have some time to look at questions 11 to 15.

3
00:00:54,721 --> 00:00:59,920
First of all, let me thank you all for coming to this public meeting to discuss the future of our town.

4
00:00:59,985 --> 00:01:04,040
Our first speaker is Shona Ferguson from Barford Town Council.

5
00:01:04,063 --> 00:01:04,263
Shona.

6
00:01:04,263 --> 00:01:04,836
from Barford Town Council.

7
00:01:04,860 --> 00:01:05,060
Shona.

8
00:01:05,091 --> 00:01:06,000
Thank you.

9
00:01:06,053 --> 00:01:09,000
First I'll briefly give you some background information.

10
00:01:09,056 --> 00:01:13,000
Then I'll be asking you for your comments on developments in the town.

11
00:01:13,075 --> 00:01:20,000
Well, as you don't need me to tell you, Barford has changed a great deal in the last 50 years.

12
00:01:20,083 --> 00:01:23,000
These are some of the main changes.

13
00:01:23,063 --> 00:01:29,446
50 years ago, buses linked virtually every part of the town and the neighbouring towns and villages.

14
00:01:29,511 --> 00:01:32,480
Most people used them frequently, but not now,

15
00:01:32,480 --> 00:01:38,080
because the bus companies concentrate on just the routes that attract most passengers.

16
00:01:38,150 --> 00:01:41,737
So parts of the town are no longer served by buses.

17
00:01:41,807 --> 00:01:49,019
Even replacing old uncomfortable buses with smart new ones has had little impact on passenger numbers.

18
00:01:49,091 --> 00:01:52,533
It's sometimes said that bus fares are too high,

19
00:01:52,533 --> 00:01:59,920
but in relation to average incomes fares are not much higher than they were 50 years ago.

20
00:01:59,978 --> 00:02:02,929
Changes in the road network are affecting the town.

21
00:02:02,987 --> 00:02:09,935
The centre was recently closed to traffic on a trial basis, making it much safer for pedestrians.

22
00:02:10,017 --> 00:02:13,040
The impact of this is being measured.

23
00:02:13,109 --> 00:02:20,509
The new cycle paths separating bikes from cars in most main roads are being used far more than was expected,

24
00:02:20,509 --> 00:02:23,355
reducing traffic and improving air quality.

25
00:02:23,420 --> 00:02:28,400
And although the council's attempts to have a bypass constructed have failed,

26
00:02:28,400 --> 00:02:32,920
we haven't given up hope of persuading the government to change its mind.

27
00:02:32,994 --> 00:02:37,040
Shopping in the town centre has changed over the years.

28
00:02:37,096 --> 00:02:41,440
Many of us can remember when the town was crowded with people going shopping.

29
00:02:41,505 --> 00:02:50,520
Numbers have been falling for several years, despite efforts to attract shoppers, for instance by opening new car parks.

30
00:02:50,584 --> 00:02:55,480
Some people combine shopping with visits to the town's restaurants and cafes.

31
00:02:55,543 --> 00:02:58,987
Most shops are small independent stores, which is good,

32
00:02:58,987 --> 00:03:04,779
but many people prefer to use supermarkets and department stores in nearby large towns,

33
00:03:04,779 --> 00:03:08,222
as there are so few well-known chain stores here.

34
00:03:08,290 --> 00:03:16,817
Turning now to medical facilities, the town is served by family doctors in several medical practices, fewer than 50 years ago,

35
00:03:16,817 --> 00:03:19,856
but each catering for far more patients.

36
00:03:19,936 --> 00:03:26,800
Our hospital closed 15 years ago, which means journeys to other towns are unavoidable.

37
00:03:26,876 --> 00:03:31,840
On the other hand, there are more dentists than there used to be.

38
00:03:31,891 --> 00:03:35,280
Employment patterns have changed along with almost everything else.

39
00:03:35,346 --> 00:03:41,200
The number of schools and colleges has increased, making that the main employment sector.

40
00:03:41,259 --> 00:03:55,000
Services such as website design and accountancy have grown in importance and surprisingly perhaps manufacturing hasn't seen the decline that has affected it in other parts of the country.

41
00:03:55,473 --> 00:04:36,640
Before you hear the rest of the talk, you have some time to look at questions 16 to 20.

42
00:04:36,697 --> 00:04:43,566
Now I'll very quickly outline current plans for some of the town's facilities, before asking for your comments.

43
00:04:43,643 --> 00:04:49,829
As you'll know if you regularly use the car pack at the railway station, it's usually full.

44
00:04:49,889 --> 00:04:56,313
The railway company applied for permission to replace it with a multi-story car pack, but that was refused.

45
00:04:56,374 --> 00:05:03,440
Instead, the company has bought some adjoining land and this will be used to increase the number of packing spaces.

46
00:05:03,503 --> 00:05:10,433
The grand, the old cinema in the High Street will close at the end of the year and reopen on a different site.

47
00:05:10,496 --> 00:05:13,780
You've probably seen the building under construction.

48
00:05:13,841 --> 00:05:21,560
The plan is to have three screens with fewer seats rather than just the one large auditorium in the old cinema.

49
00:05:21,629 --> 00:05:24,894
I expect many of you shop in the indoor market.

50
00:05:24,964 --> 00:05:32,000
It's become more and more shabby looking and because of fears about safety it was threatened with demolition.

51
00:05:32,061 --> 00:05:40,390
The good news is that it will close for six weeks to be made safe and redecorated and the improved building will open in July.

52
00:05:40,465 --> 00:05:47,000
Lots of people use the library, including school and college students who go there to study.

53
00:05:47,058 --> 00:05:53,000
The council has managed to secure funding to keep the library open later into the evening twice a week.

54
00:05:53,068 --> 00:06:00,000
We would like to enlarge the building in the not too distant future, but this is by no means definite.

55
00:06:00,057 --> 00:06:06,320
There is no limit on access to the nature reserve on the edge of town, and this will continue to be the case.

56
00:06:06,381 --> 00:06:11,600
What will change, though, is that the council will no longer be in charge of the area.

57
00:06:11,663 --> 00:06:19,520
Instead, it will become the responsibility of a national body that administers most nature reserves in the country.

58
00:06:19,590 --> 00:06:26,320
Okay, now let me ask you if you have...

59
00:06:26,424 --> 00:06:29,440
That is the end of section 2.

60
00:06:29,937 --> 00:06:54,289
You now have half a minute to check your answers.

61
00:06:54,786 --> 00:07:05,720
Now turn to section 3.